{
  "duration": 84.699,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.059,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.839,
      "end": 3.759,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.299,
      "end": 5.039,
      "text": "Now in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.5,
      "end": 8.3,
      "text": "a passenger is sitting inside a train moving at"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.76,
      "end": 10.8,
      "text": "thirty-six kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.399,
      "end": 12.779,
      "text": "He sees another train of length"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.199,
      "end": 17.459,
      "text": "one hundred eighty meters coming from the opposite direction at fifty-four kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.02,
      "end": 22.799,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find how much time the other train takes to completely pass the passenger."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.199,
      "end": 24.459,
      "text": "Now, the important point here is"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.879,
      "end": 27.439,
      "text": "that the passenger is treated as a point."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.84,
      "end": 29.219,
      "text": "Since a passenger has no length,"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.599,
      "end": 31.76,
      "text": "the other train only needs to cover its own length,"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.159,
      "end": 33.799,
      "text": "which is one hundred eighty meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.5,
      "end": 36.399,
      "text": "The trains are moving in opposite directions."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.719,
      "end": 37.459,
      "text": "What does that mean?"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.799,
      "end": 39.379,
      "text": "It means their speeds add up."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.779,
      "end": 42.739,
      "text": "So the relative speed will be thirty-six plus fifty-four"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.459,
      "end": 45.419,
      "text": "equals ninety kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.039,
      "end": 50.479,
      "text": "Now we need the speed in meter per second. So ninety times five by eighteen"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.139,
      "end": 53.059,
      "text": "equals twenty-five meters per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.559,
      "end": 53.859,
      "text": "Done."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.559,
      "end": 55.779,
      "text": "Now we have everything we need."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.5,
      "end": 60.879,
      "text": "We know distance equals length of the other train equals one hundred eighty meters."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.359,
      "end": 63.859,
      "text": "Relative speed equals twenty-five meters per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.4,
      "end": 65.239,
      "text": "Using the formula,"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.699,
      "end": 68.099,
      "text": "time equals distance divided by speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 68.639,
      "end": 75.459,
      "text": "So time equals one hundred eighty divided by twenty-five. After calculating this, we get time equals seven point two seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 76.239,
      "end": 81.979,
      "text": "Hence, the other train takes seven point two seconds to completely pass the passenger."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.479,
      "end": 84.699,
      "text": "So the correct option is option D."
    }
  ],
